<http://data.silknow.org/event/c6e1ebdb-cdde-33c1-ae8f-bb977c919f8a>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "From Miss Reckitt's original letter of 16/04/1923 (RF 23/2916): Our family have a number of dresses of the period between 1856 & 1886 - perfectly fresh and clean except two muslins, & some, I should say, never worn.  There are about two silk ones the others are silk & mohair - alpaca & bright ally of very lasting quality.  Probably they are good \"middle class\" bought at Peter Robinsons, Duncan Smiths -  Marshall & Snelgrove or Lewis & Allenbys.\"  It is evident from the RF that Miss Reckitt gave no history of the garments, and may well have known none."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/444afea0-3942-30dc-b0e8-008c620b9eaf> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Miss Juliet Reckitt and Messrs G. F. and A. L. Reckitt" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/336b0cef-7133-3a22-af69-44ba1015a913> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "From Miss Reckitt's original letter of 16/04/1923 (RF 23/2916): Our family have a number of dresses of the period between 1856 & 1886 - perfectly fresh and clean except two muslins, & some, I should say, never worn.  There are about two silk ones the others are silk & mohair - alpaca & bright ally of very lasting quality.  Probably they are good \"middle class\" bought at Peter Robinsons, Duncan Smiths -  Marshall & Snelgrove or Lewis & Allenbys.\"  It is evident from the RF that Miss Reckitt gave no history of the garments, and may well have known none."@en .

